duckdb: build for WASI.

Leave out what WASI doesn't have: other processes (kill), the CPU a
thread runs on (sched_getcpu), resource limits (getrlimit) and file
locks (so, as with SQLite, a database file mustn't be shared between
processes). The terminal width comes from pywasi's terminal support
(<termios.h>).

--- a/external/duckdb/src/common/process_util.cpp
+++ b/external/duckdb/src/common/process_util.cpp
@@ -59,6 +59,9 @@
 	auto running = GetExitCodeProcess(process, &exit_code) && exit_code == STILL_ACTIVE;
 	CloseHandle(process);
 	return running;
+#elif defined(__wasi__)
+	// No processes to look up (WASI): only this one.
+	return pid == getpid();
 #else
 	// EPERM means it exists and belongs to somebody else
 	return kill(static_cast<pid_t>(pid), 0) == 0 || errno == EPERM;
